*   **Schedule B (Interest and Ordinary Dividends):** Because your combined interest ($1,120) and dividends ($510) exceed $1,500, the IRS requires you to fill out Schedule B.
*   **Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business):** To report your $19,700 in 1099-NEC income and deduct your work supplies.
*   **Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home):** You will need this form if you choose the "Actual Expenses" method for your home office deduction.
*   **Schedule SE (Self-Employment Tax):** To calculate the Social Security and Medicare taxes owed on your net freelance profit.

*Note: You will also need to file a Minnesota state tax return, which will start with your federal adjusted gross income but may have different rules for certain deductions.*

